 "line_count_note": "30 ruled lines, all 30 carrying a NAME. The schema-1 reading's figure of 30 is restated unchanged, and the cells confirm it — see line_count_finding.",
 "line_count_finding": "THE 30-versus-31 QUESTION IS SETTLED BY THE SHEET'S OWN ARITHMETIC, and it was worth more than the cells. PR #670 carries 31 rows for printed page 229; the sheet carries 30 ruled entries. Seventeen of the nineteen columns that carry a mark on this page CLOSE EXACTLY on the 30 lines read here — free white males 1,2,3,4,5,7,8,9,10 and free white females 15,16,17,18,19,20,21,22 — against the figures the enumerator footed at the bottom of his own sheet. A 31st household would have had to put its people somewhere, and there is nowhere left: every balanced column is already full at 30 lines. So the sheet has 30 entries and at least one of #670's 31 rows for this page has no line to sit on, which is what crosswalk_670.json's row_offset_test could only suspect. Nothing here says WHICH #670 row is the intruder. A second finding sits beside it: line 26 — R. D. Coe — is a NAMED head with no mark in any of the 38 columns — a household of nobody — and the two columns that do not balance are not the reason, because neither carries a mark on line 26 either.",
